$\blueD{\text{Line }a}$ has points at $(2,5)$ and $(7,8)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{8-5}{7-2} \\\\\\
&={\dfrac{3}{5}}
\end{align}$

$\greenD{\text{Line }b}$ has points at $(-7,-9)$ and $(3,-2)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{-2-(-9)}{3-(-7)} \\\\\\
&= {\dfrac{7}{10}}
\end{align}$
